cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VERDICT: Evidence-First Indirect Control Flow Recovery"
version: 0.9.0
date-released: 2026-10-11
url: https://github.com/vasquezbrandon205/verdict
repository-code: https://github.com/vasquezbrandon205/verdict
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Vasquez
    given-names: Brandon Manuel
keywords:
  - binary-analysis
  - reverse-engineering
  - indirect-calls
  - control-flow-recovery
  - falsification
abstract: >
  Independent binary analysis engine (zero Ghidra dependency: custom ELF
  loader, Capstone decoder, built-from-scratch CFG) for recovering indirect
  call targets in stripped, optimized binaries. Kill-aware dataflow, vtable
  slot analysis, SIMD lane tracking, interprocedural inference, and
  cross-module resolution -- each producing explicit evidence chains.
  Zero-false-positive gating with honest UNKNOWN abstention instead of
  silent misses.
